The advantage of resolutions computed from A-infinity structures is the
decomposition of the differential into blocks corresponding to tensor products
of the modules in the finite resolutions. In the following display, the symbol
{u_1..u_n} denotes B_(u_1)**..**B_(u_(n-1))**G_(u_n), where G is the S-free
resolution of M and B is the truncated shift of the S-free resolution A of R^1:
that is, B_i = A_(i-1), i = 2...length A.

