displayBlocks -- prints a matrix showing the source and target decomposition
****************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        displayBlocks M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, with source and target
        labeled direct sums of free modules

Description
===========

The maps produced by *note burkeResolution: burkeResolution, and *note
aInfinity: aInfinity, have direct sums of labeled modules as sources and
targets; the label corresponds to the tensor factors.

displayBlocks M shows this data

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a,b,c]/(ideal(a,b,c^2))^2                                    |
